    {
      "page_title": "Why Generics: Generic Functions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is a Generic?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Generics== are type parameters: types passed in like arguments",
            "Written in angle brackets: `<T>`",
            "Erased at compile time: **zero** runtime cost",
            "`T` is only a type, never usable as a value"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Problem and the Fix",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function identity(x: any): any {",
            "  return x;",
            "}",
            "const n = identity(5); // any"
          ],
          "note": "caller gets any back"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function identity<T>(x: T): T {",
            "  return x;",
            "}",
            "const s = identity(\"a\"); // \"a\""
          ],
          "note": "T links input to output"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "T is",
            "How"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`identity<string>('a')`",
              "string",
              "explicit"
            ],
            [
              "`identity('a')`",
              "'a'",
              "literal inferred"
            ],
            [
              "`let v = identity('a')`",
              "string",
              "widened at let"
            ],
            [
              "`const v = identity('a')`",
              "'a'",
              "literal kept"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function id<const T>(x: T): T {",
            "  return x;",
            "}",
            "id(\"a\"); // type is \"a\""
          ],
          "note": "const T keeps the literal"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. More Than One Param",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function pair<A, B>(a: A, b: B)",
            "  : [A, B] {",
            "  return [a, b];",
            "}",
            "pair(1, \"x\"); // [number, string]"
          ],
          "note": "each param inferred on its own"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`<T>(x: T) => x` in `.tsx` parses as JSX",
            "Write `<T,>` or `<T extends unknown>` instead"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Examples: Dry Run",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function first<T>(arr: T[])",
            "  : T | undefined {",
            "  return arr[0];",
            "}",
            "function map<T, U>(arr: T[],",
            "  fn: (x: T) => U): U[] { ... }"
          ],
          "note": "map infers T and U from call"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Union version: pass a `string`, get back `string | number`",
            "Generic version: pass a `string`, get back `string`"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "If a type parameter appears only **once** in a signature, it is probably not needed."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Quick test",
          "text": "Ask: does T connect two places in the signature? If not, use a plain type."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "typescript",
      "subtitle": "Type parameters 101"
    },
    {
