          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Generics vs Unions",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Signature",
            "in → out linked?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`(x: string | number) => string | number`",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`<T extends string | number>(x: T): T`",
              "yes"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "declare const u: (x: string | number)",
            "  => string | number;",
            "declare function g<T extends",
            "  string | number>(x: T): T;",
            "u(\"a\"); // string | number",
            "g(\"a\"); // \"a\""
          ],
          "note": "union forgets which one came in"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. When to Skip Generics",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`log<T>(x: T): void` is just `(x: unknown) => void`",
            "T used **once** adds noise, no link between types",
            "Lint rule `no-unnecessary-type-parameters` flags it",
            "Generic only when the output depends on the input"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Generics vs unknown",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Reach for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Only pass a value around",
              "`unknown`"
            ],
            [
              "Output depends on input",
              "generic `<T>`"
            ],
            [
              "Clean per-case signatures",
              "overloads"
            ],
            [
              "Key lookup on an object",
              "`<T, K extends keyof T>`"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "function show(x: unknown): void {",
            "  console.log(x);",
            "}",
            "function same<T>(x: T): T {",
            "  return x;",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "unknown for pass-through only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Five type params nobody can read: prefer simple overloads",
            "Overloads give clean per-case signatures",
            "Generics with conditionals: one signature, ==weaker== body check"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Count the uses",
          "text": "Find where T appears. Once means swap it for `unknown` or its bound."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`new T()` and `typeof T` do not compile",
            "Pass a constructor or a tag value instead",
            "`return {} as T` hides a **real** bug"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`Object.keys`, `JSON.parse`, `Object.entries` lose generics",
            "Cast at **one** small boundary, not everywhere",
            "Check the shape at runtime before you cast"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Test your types",
          "text": "Type-level code needs tests too: use `expectTypeOf` or `tsd`."
        }
      ],
