      "page_title": "Generic Interfaces & Classes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is It?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Generic interface==: `interface Box<T> { value: T }`",
            "Use it as `Box<number>`; T is filled in by you",
            "Generic ==type alias== takes params the same way",
            "Generic function type: `type Mapper<T, U> = (x: T) => U`"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "interface Box<T> { value: T }",
            "const b: Box<number> = { value: 5 };",
            "type Mapper<T, U> = (x: T) => U;",
            "const len: Mapper<string, number> =",
            "  s => s.length;"
          ],
          "note": "T is fixed at the use site"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Alias with Two Params",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type Result<T, E> =",
            "  | { ok: true; value: T }",
            "  | { ok: false; error: E };",
            "const r: Result<number, string> =",
            "  { ok: true, value: 1 };"
          ],
          "note": "Alias can express unions"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : `Props<T> = { items: T[]; render: (item: T) => string }` is the React-style list prop. One T links items to render.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Classes and Inference",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "class Stack<T> {",
            "  private items: T[] = [];",
            "  push(x: T) { this.items.push(x); }",
            "  pop(): T | undefined {",
            "    return this.items.pop();",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "T belongs to each instance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
