          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Default as Fallback",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "declare function mk<T = string>",
            "  (): T;",
            "const a = mk(); // string",
            "const b = mk<number>(); // number"
          ],
          "note": "default beats unknown, loses to explicit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default fills in only when nothing else supplies T",
            "Explicit args and inference candidates both beat it",
            "A default is ==not== a bound: it does not restrict T"
