    {
      "page_title": "Conditional Types & Distribution",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A ==conditional type== picks one of two types, **at the type level**: `T extends U ? X : Y`. If T is assignable to U you get X, else Y.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type IsString<T> =",
            "  T extends string ? true : false;",
            "type A = IsString<'hi'>;  // true",
            "type B = IsString<42>;    // false"
          ],
          "note": "resolved by the compiler, not at runtime"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Distribution",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A **naked** type parameter splits a union across its members",
            "Each member is checked alone, results are unioned",
            "Wrap as `[T] extends [U]` to ==block distribution==",
            "`never` is the empty union, so a distributive conditional over it gives `never`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type ToArray<T> =",
            "  T extends any ? T[] : never;",
            "type D = ToArray<string|number>;",
            "// string[] | number[]",
            "type N = ToArray<never>; // never"
          ],
          "note": "naked T distributes over unions"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Input",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "T extends U",
              "string | number",
              "per member"
            ],
            [
              "[T] extends [U]",
              "string | number",
              "one check"
            ],
            [
              "T extends U",
              "never",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "[T] extends [U]",
              "never",
              "one check, no split"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. infer: capture a type",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`infer U` declares a ==type variable== inside the extends clause and fills it from the match. Use it only on the true branch.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ts",
          "lines": [
            "type El<T> =",
            "  T extends Array<infer U> ? U : never;",
            "type E = El<string[]>; // string",
            "type RT<F> = F extends",
            "  (...a: any[]) => infer R ? R : never;"
          ],
          "note": "infer R reads the return position"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "infer picks",
            "Example in → out"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(infer A)[]",
              "element",
              "number[] → number"
            ],
            [
              "(...a: infer P) => any",
              "param tuple",
              "(x: string) => 1 → [string]"
            ],
            [
              "Promise<infer U>",
              "resolved",
              "Promise<Date> → Date"
            ],
            [
              "[infer H, ...any[]]",
              "first item",
              "[1, 2] → 1"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Naked T splits unions; [T] keeps them whole. infer captures; extends narrows."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "typescript",
      "subtitle": "types that branch"
    },
